1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,850
Charts turn information into clues.

2
00:00:02,950 --> 00:00:04,980
Let us read them!

3
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:07,877
Read the picture key first.

4
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:11,373
If one symbol means two children,

5
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:15,814
two symbols and a half mean five children.

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:21,300
A different key may give one book symbol ten books.

7
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:24,980
Then half a symbol means five books.

8
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:27,877
For bars, read the scale.

9
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:32,268
Halfway between twelve and sixteen is fourteen.

10
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:35,400
This bar shows fourteen visitors.

11
00:00:35,450 --> 00:00:37,086
Another shows eight.

12
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:41,814
Subtract to find the difference: six more visitors.

13
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:46,918
A line chart tracks change over time.

14
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:51,100
Read the dots against the height scale.

15
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:54,850
Growing from four centimeters to nine centimeters

16
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:57,627
means five centimeters of growth.

17
00:00:57,700 --> 00:01:00,427
Height and growth are different.

18
00:01:01,150 --> 00:01:05,050
A pie chart shows parts of a whole.

19
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:08,650
Thirty-two children split into eight equal parts

20
00:01:08,700 --> 00:01:10,650
means four per part.

21
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:12,882
Half means sixteen children;

22
00:01:13,050 --> 00:01:15,232
one quarter means eight.

23
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:20,750
To compare Orange team’s events,

24
00:01:20,800 --> 00:01:24,600
choose Event for what the bars show,

25
00:01:24,650 --> 00:01:26,832
then filter to Orange.

26
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:32,855
Sort most first to put the largest score on top.

27
00:01:33,250 --> 00:01:36,523
Switch to Table for exact numbers;

28
00:01:36,620 --> 00:01:39,347
the data stays the same.

29
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:41,600
Which event is first?

30
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:47,782
Skipping, with eleven points.

31
00:01:50,150 --> 00:01:53,423
Check the key, scale, and question.

32
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:56,207
Choose the view you need,

33
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:59,553
then try the Unit Four quizzes!
